# Methodological Framing

Here’s how you would write this in a thesis:

> A shallow CNN baseline was first implemented to establish centralized performance. However, due to limited representational capacity and severe class imbalance, minority class recall remained poor.
>
> To address imbalance, class-weighted cross entropy was introduced, which improved minority recall but reduced overall accuracy due to model capacity constraints.
>
> Replacing the shallow CNN with a pretrained ResNet18 backbone significantly improved both macro F1-score and minority class recall, demonstrating that architectural depth and transfer learning are critical for fine-grained DR severity classification.

This is clean experimental reasoning.

