# Now Link This to Federated Learning

Here’s the important conceptual bridge:

Federated Learning (FL) introduces:

* Non-IID data across clients
* Data fragmentation
* Smaller local datasets
* Amplified imbalance

In FL:

* Some hospitals may have mostly class 0
* Some may rarely see class 3
* Local models become biased
* Global aggregation may underrepresent rare classes

If centralized CNN struggles with minority classes,
federated shallow CNN will struggle more.

Your ResNet result tells us:

> Strong backbone is required before federated training.

Because FL will reduce effective data per client.

